module ord-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

// The District of Oregon's local criminal rules. The vendored text is
// CURRENCY UNCONFIRMED (sources/fed-dor/PROVENANCE.md), so no period,
// limit or amount is taken from it: each period below is named with the
// rule that sets it and is not stated. The events are the triggers those
// periods run from, so a later pass over a dated edition can encode them.
//
// Holes (not stated; currency unconfirmed): the earliest sentencing date
// after a guilty plea or verdict (Crim. LR 32-1); the filing of the
// presentence report with its addendum before sentencing (Crim. LR 32-1);
// a defendant's notice to the Clerk's Office and the Marshal that the
// defendant wishes to appear by video teleconference, and another party's
// request for the defendant's consent to a VTC appearance, before the
// hearing (Crim. LR 43-2(a), (b)), both waivable for exigent matters (Crim.
// LR 43-2(c)); and the delivery of a judge's paper copy after electronic
// filing (Crim. LR 49-7).
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp: the probation
// officer's disclosure of the presentence report "consistent with Fed. R.
// Crim. P. 32(e)(2)" and the objection period of FRCrimP 32(f), which the
// parties may waive with the Court's approval (Crim. LR 32-1).
//
// The rules without a period stay unencoded: disclosure of a sealed
// charging document to defense counsel (Crim. LR 5), sentencing
// stipulations (Crim. LR 11-1), CJA subpoenas and witness nondisclosure
// (Crim. LR 17-1, 17-2), presentence-report confidentiality (Crim. LR
// 32-2), VTC authorization and consent (Crim. LR 43-1, 43-3), electronic
// filing and service (Crim. LR 49), redaction (Crim. LR 49.1) and
// collateral forfeiture (Crim. LR 58-1).
//
// The earlier D. Or. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// belong to lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is
// vendored.
/// A guilty plea is entered or a guilty verdict returned (D. Or. Crim. LR
/// 32-1).
event GuiltyPleaOrVerdict()
/// The sentencing date is set (D. Or. Crim. LR 32-1).
event SentencingDateSet()
/// A hearing is set at which a defendant may appear by video
/// teleconference (D. Or. Crim. LR 43-2).
event VtcHearingScheduled()
/// A document for which a judge's paper copy is required is filed
/// electronically (D. Or. Crim. LR 49-7).
event JudgesCopyDocumentFiled()
